{
  "dom_id": "step-q96486",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.005.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.5758)=0.995.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.5758)=1-0.995=0.005.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.5758)=0.005.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14263990/assets/23e806ce7589f0d262df8551d21e11850196b13fe05499525ed8caf2b78edbbe.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.5758) & =0.005 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.5758) & =0.005.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.5758.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
